  "issue_number": 103,
  "issue_title": "feat(submission): offline preflight validator for routing-head packs (gates 1-5)",
  "issue_body": "**Problem**\n\nAnti-cheat gates 1-4 live only inside the 850-line maintainer script ``scripts/pr_eval.py``. Miners discover rate-limit, weight-shape, duplicate-head, and receipt-plausibility failures **after** opening a PR. There is no importable module and no miner-facing CLI to run the same checks offline (no GPU, no OpenRouter).\n\nA fifth gap: ``receipt.json`` ``total_cost_usd`` is never cross-checked against a verified ``TRINITY_COST_LEDGER`` total, so a fabricated receipt can disagree with the append-only ledger while still passing gate 4.\n\n**Proposed solution**\n\n1. Add ``trinity.submission`` \u2014 ``SubmissionPack`` loader, ``SubmissionGate`` classes, ``PreflightRunner``.\n2. Add ``scripts/preflight_submission.py`` so miners can run gates locally before pushing.\n3. Refactor ``pr_eval.py`` to import the shared gates; add gate 5 (ledger/receipt cost consistency).\n4. Add ``trinity.llm.openrouter_pricing`` so ``cost_report.py``, ``pack_submission.py``, and gate 5 share per-model in/out rates.\n5. Offline tests in ``tests/test_submission_preflight.py``.\n\n**Acceptance**\n\n- [ ] ``python scripts/preflight_submission.py --submission miner/1`` exits 0 on a valid pack\n- [ ] Duplicate / bad receipt / ledger mismatch fail locally with the same reason strings as pr_eval\n- [ ] ``pytest tests/test_submission_preflight.py`` passes without GPU or network\n\n**Environment**\n\n- Python 3.11, CPU only\n- Commit: `5f02a7c`",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-10T19:31:58.000Z",
  "test_cmd": [
    "python",
    "-m",
    "pytest",
    "--tb=short",
